q2. Q19. Analyze the code block below and determine the final value of sum and why.
int[] a = {1, 2, 3};
int sum = 0;

for(int i : a) {
    if(i == 2)
        continue;


    sum += i;
}

sum = 4;
Why?
The continue statement skips the current iteration when i equals 2. Therefore, only 1 and 3 are added to sum.
sum = 1 + 3 = 4

Q3. A Java class contains multiple constructors. Explain how the compiler determines which constructor to execute when an object is 
instantiated.
Constructor Overloading
The compiler matches the constructor call with the constructor whose parameter list (number, type, and order of parameters)
best matches the arguments provided.

